        "text": {
            "description_html": "<b>Fusion BU-G9, Rock Ridge Collection Sandcast Brass Nevada Lever with Comstock Rose</b>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nPart of Fusion's Rock Ridge Collection, the Nevada Lever with Rectangular Rose is featured with an oil rubbed bronze finish. It is available in dummy, passage and privacy functions. This Nevada Leverset is made to fit doors with backsets of either 2-3/8 inches or 2-3/4 inches and will adjust to fit doors 1-1/4 inches to 2 inches thick.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Sandcasting</b> is a process for casting metal in sand molds. The mold is made by packing the sand around a pattern. Molten brass is then poured into a mold cavity formed out of sand. Each sand mold is used only once. The sand is then recycled for the next piece.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Features</b> for the Fusion BU Nevada Lever with G9 Comstock Rose:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Solid Brass Construction</li>\r\n<li>Cycle Tested to ANSI Standards</li>\r\n<li>Reversible Latchbolt in matching/coordinating finish</li>\r\n<li>Easy assembly with alignment block and rose posts</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Specifications</b> for the Sandcast Brass Nevada Lever with Rectangular Comstock Rose:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Finish: <b>Oil Rubbed Bronze</b></li>\r\n<li>Lever Length: 4-1/8\"</li>\r\n<li>Lever Projection: 1-7/8\"</li>\r\n<li>Rose Length: 4-1/4\"</li>\r\n<li>Rose Width: 2-5/8\"</li>\r\n<li>Rose Projection: 1/2”</li>\r\n<li>Door Thickness: 1-1/4\" to 2\"</li>\r\n<li>Backsets: Either 2-3/8\" or 2-3/4\"</li>\r\n<li>Material: Sandcast Brass</li>\r\n<li>Standard Latch Rotation is 40 Degrees.</li>\r\n<li>Square corner latches and strike plates </li>\r\n<li>Lifetime Limited Warranty on workmanship, materials, and operation.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>When Selecting a Function:</b>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><b>Single Dummy:</b> Non-functional pull to match trim on one side of the door. Just for looks, it does not latch and does not lock.</li>\r\n<li><b>Dummy Set:</b> Non-functional pull to match trim on both sides of the door. Just for looks, it does not latch and does not lock.</li>\r\n<li><b>Passage (Hall or Closet):</b> For doors that don't need locking.</li>\r\n<li><b>Privacy (Bedroom or Bathroom):</b> For doors that could need locking.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>",
